1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.600
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:38.910
<b>Interception</b>

12
00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.590
Well, Stella,
 you can’t just start talking out of nowhere.

13
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.720
Hmm? What do you mean, Shaka?

14
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.230
People will need to be
 prepared to listen to you, surely.

15
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.230
What? What’s going on?

16
00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.940
You really think that’s necessary...?

17
00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.310
Some intelligence agency will pick this up,

18
00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.650
and by the next day it’ll have
 spread around the world...

19
00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:56.740
Are you certain about that?

20
00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.570
What if they manipulate the information?

21
00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.080
You do have a point...

22
00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.740
So what do we do, then?

23
00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.710
Using the Navy branches all over the world
 as relays,

24
00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.130
we’ll force them to broadcast us over the brainwaves at maximum output.

25
00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.550
The hell is this?!
Where’s this signal coming from?!

26
00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:17.420
Through all Snails, sir! Fleet-wide!

27
00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.640
Kill that signal!
Kill it now!

28
00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.140
B-But...

29
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.850
...I can’t, sir!

30
00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.350
Transponder Snails will be able to
 receive audio signals,

31
00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.190
but setting up the Video Transponder Snails
 may take some time...

32
00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.030
I suggest a wait time of one hour.

33
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.490
What is it you intend to
tell the world, Vegapunk...?

34
00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.870
An hour?!

35
00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.200
That seems long! So long, in fact...

36
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.290
Hey, yo, isn’t this...?

37
00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.420
It’s Vegapunk, right?

38
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.000
From where, though?
And why now?

39
00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.630
Fire!

40
00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.780
...that it will give those who do not want
 this message to be heard

41
00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.510
the time to sabotage it.

42
00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.390
All right, very well!

43
00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.900
Let’s make the prep time
 for receiving our message...

44
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.820
...ten minutes!

45
00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.230
You hear that, world?!

46
00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.900
Hey! Why am I hearing your voice,

47
00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.700
Vegapunk?!

48
00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:29.640
<b>Holy Land
Mary Geoise</b>

49
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.910
What is this broadcast-eh?!

50
00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.540
What is going on-eh?!

51
00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.290
Hey, Saturn...
What happened to Vegapunk?

52
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.710
Kizaru killed him.

53
00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.420
He should be dead.

54
00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.760
Ah...

55
00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.510
That is what I believe.

56
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.720
I watched him die.

57
00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:49.140
Did he arrange for this message
to transmit upon his death?

58
00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.680
It would appear so...

59
00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.640
What he will say, however,
is unknown to us...

60
00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.310
If only we could find
the source of the broadcast...

61
00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.730
It cannot be anywhere else
but the Labophase on Egghead.

62
00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.950
It is currently protected by the barrier...

63
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.830
So, nine and a half minutes of waiting...
 Want to invent something in the meantime?

64
00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.990
I’m rather busy.

65
00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.520
Why not have some coffee?

66
00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.330
<b>Dressrosa
New World</b>

67
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.840
Hey, did you hear?!

68
00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.000
This is huge!

69
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.300
The Dr. Vegapunk
is trying to tell the entire world something!

70
00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.220
What?!

71
00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.350
Bring the Video Transponder Snail!

72
00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.890
Set up the screen!

73
00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.430
This way, move it! We don’t have time!

74
00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.060
Calculating probability of
 signal jamming...

75
00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.860
Rebecca, the picture’s coming in now.

76
00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.280
That’s...

77
00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.110
...Vegapunk?

78
00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.620
Leo! Kabu!

79
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.160
Are you here to watch the broadcast?

80
00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.460
Dat da pwofessor
Luffyland tooked hostage?!

81
00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.000
What’s goin’ on over dere?

82
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.750
Huh?

83
00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.340
Oh, Leo...
You really believe that bad press about Lucy?

84
00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:08.640
<b>Windmill Village
East Blue</b>

85
00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:14.930
The heck? I thought the news was about
Luffy being up to no good again.

86
00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.190
Too bad we don’t have
a Video Transponder Snail...

87
00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:22.020
Can’t we get one for the village,
Mayor? Pretty please?

88
00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.280
And who’s gonna pay for it?!

89
00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.460
Just raisin’ those things costs money, you know!

90
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.530
Long’s we got sound, that’s plenty!

91
00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.410
Awwwwh!

92
00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.060
<b>Water Seven
Grand Line</b>

93
00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.540
Wake up!

94
00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.950
This is serious!

95
00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.960
Hrmm...

96
00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.210
Alice...

97
00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.790
Yes, President.

98
00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:44.130
Set up the Video Transponder Snail
right away.

99
00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.840
Already receiving in the next room, sir.

100
00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:53.160
<b>Iceberg's secretary
Alice</b>

101
00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.640
You’re ahead of the game, as usual...

102
00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.500
It may be the middle of the night,

103
00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:56.980
but given the apparent importance of this event,

104
00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:59.080
I’ve delegated contact of all residents

105
00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.440
so they can be ready to watch within ten minutes.

106
00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.400
Anything else?

107
00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.380
<b>World Economic
Journal</b>

108
00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:06.570
What the?!

109
00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.030
What’s this video about?!

110
00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:11.570
It’s being relayed via Navy branches,
but it’s an independent signal!

111
00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:15.540
What do you mean?
Then where are Luffy-san and the others now?

112
00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.290
Look at the clock behind them, ya dunce.

113
00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.960
That ain’t the current time on Egghead.

114
00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.960
This footage is previously recorded!

115
00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:29.180
It should be the scene of an inferno by now,
courtesy of a Buster Call!

116
00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:32.740
<b>West Blue</b>

117
00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.600
Is this the real Dr. Vegapunk?!

118
00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.100
I heard his mind’s so sharp,
it cut its way out of his head!

119
00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.960
<b>North Blue</b>

120
00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:45.020
The man with the biggest brain in the world,
who brought light to us all...

121
00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.880
<b>South Blue</b>

122
00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:49.450
What’s so important that
he’s gotta tell the whole world?!

123
00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.110
Maybe it’s the greatest invention of
the century?

124
00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.180
<b>Kamabakka Queendom</b>

125
00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:59.830
It’ll take ten minutes to brew the coffee.

126
00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.080
I won’t have time to drink it!

127
00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.750
Hmmm, hmmm...

128
00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.880
The probability of signal jamming
 is extremely low.

129
00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.670
What is Vegapunk doing?!

130
00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.180
But more importantly,

131
00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:14.300
his head!

132
00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.180
His mind’s gotten too sharp for it!

133
00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:18.860
He’s the Doctor Vegapunk

134
00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:20.850
I’ve heard lots about
who multiplied himself?!

135
00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.810
I thought he was being held hostage!

136
00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:27.190
He can do this in the middle of
that kind of situation?

137
00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:32.860
I suspect...

138
00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.480
...that my death is imminent.

139
00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:44.880
<b>Egghead
North-western side</b>

140
00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.250
Almost there!

141
00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:49.880
I’ve spotted it!

142
00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.930
Yeah, that’s right!

143
00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:56.390
That’s our ship!

144
00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.600
The Great Erik!

145
00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.440
Vegapunk and the others...
Wonder if they’re doing okay...

146
00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:14.990
Punchin’ ya ain’t doin’ squat, huh?

147
00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.250
As long as any of my crew
are still on the island...

148
00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:30.300
You guys ain’t goin’ nowhere!

149
00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.800
Gum-Gum...

150
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.890
...Dawn...

151
00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:42.390
...Cymbal!

152
00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:55.610
If yer just gonna keep comin’ back
from whatever I do to ya...

153
00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.450
How ‘bout I just...

154
00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:02.290
...send ya flyin’, one-way!

155
00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.420
There’s something in the air...
Incoming!

156
00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.940
Whaaaa?!

157
00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.780
Why’s nothin’ I’m doin’ hurtin’ him?!

158
00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:46.000
Go away!

159
00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.840
Kizaru, sir?
What just happened...?

160
00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.000
Are you okay, sir?!

161
00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.010
Admiral!

162
00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:09.140
We do not have time, Saturn!

163
00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.520
Vegapunk must not...

164
00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.980
...be given license to speak!

165
00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.030
Oh, that was close!

166
00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:25.540
Whoa! Yikes! Eek!

167
00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:44.300
Oof... Hup!

168
00:10:58.280 --> 00:10:59.780
I shall make the summons.

169
00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.030
Very good.

170
00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:46.450
Huh?! What is...?

171
00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.410
Black lightning?!

172
00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.620
What’s that?!

173
00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:09.260
That’s exactly like
when the Spider Geezer emerged...!

174
00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:32.980
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

175
00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:37.200
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop beep-beep-beep-bup-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipii pipopii, pipopiipii

176
00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:41.410
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

177
00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:43.890
Beep-bup-beep
Piipapii papipo, piipapii

178
00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.940
No No No No No norenai

179
00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:49.020
No, no, no, no, no, not feelin' it

180
00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:53.180
kobiritsuichatte mou odorenai

181
00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:53.220
I'm all stiff, all outta dances

182
00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:57.460
My head feels so good, 'f I get unlucky again
atama Feel so good, mata Unlucky demo

183
00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:01.560
Cola de fukitobase yowaki o
just gonna blow away the shy with a cola

184
00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:05.640
Hey all you boys & girls! Looking good!
soko no Boys & Girls! omae ii yatsu

185
00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:09.190
Hey all you boys & girls!
soko no Boys & Girls!

186
00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.160
Update failed. I've had enough!
appudeto wa shippai kori gori

187
00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:15.040
Wasn't it OK 'til yesterday?
kinou made nara seikai?

188
00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:21.370
La la la la la la, run, run, run...
ran ran ran ran ran ran Run Run Run

189
00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:25.090
"Hiding yet?"
mou ii kai?

190
00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:27.460
You ready yet, up for a dance
junbi wa douyo odoreru no?

191
00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:29.830
bukkowareteru kono jidai
in this broken era?

192
00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:33.510
"Come find us!"
mou ii yo!

193
00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:35.860
Spread out from here, drop into the world
koko kara kakusan sekai e Drop

194
00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:38.260
Let loose on the stage of freedom and liberation
jiyuu to kaihou no Stage e

195
00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.490
Those rising heads're punks!!!!!! No way!!!
wakiagaru atama ga Punk!!!!!! No way!!!

196
00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:42.440
Sick of waitin', goof off and dance
matenaiyo fuzaketa Dance

197
00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.420
Dopamine spilling over
afuredasu dopamin

198
00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.660
The lonely singing in unity
kodoku ga tsudoi utau koushin

199
00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.760
Bip-bip-bip-bup-bup-bup-bup-bupping
pipipi papapapapatteru

200
00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.720
Can't can't can't count me out yet
mada mada mada horobinai

201
00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:53.170
There's some stranger waving me over
shiranai dareka ga temaneki da

202
00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:55.910
Smilin' so wide that it can't be real
uso mitai ni waratteru
